= Pins and themes

One selection per match, edited at once: the Helix way.

== Challenge 5

Make Musubi yours:

+ *Pin* this note: the pin button shows when the pointer is over its row in
  the explorer (`Space e` shows or hides it). It appears under _Pinned_, on
  every copy of your vault. The last notes you opened are under _Recent_,
  and every note under _Notebook_.
+ Open the *settings* with `Space ,` and try the *GitHub Dark* theme with
  the arrows. Keep it, or go back to _Follow the system_. Autosave is there
  too.
+ *Split* the window with `Space w v`: two panes, `Space w w` moves between
  them, `Space w q` closes one.

The next step is in the *graph* of the links: press `Space g`, find the note
named _Writing Typst_ and click it. `Space g` again leaves the graph.

Back to the #note-link("Welcome/Helix_workshop")[workshop].
